{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Cardboard box of paintbrushes (with lid): 21 paintbrushes bundled in three (3) groups with rubber bands by manufacturer; 4 - El Greco brushes, 5 - \"Mussini\" Grumbacher brushes, 11- Rubens brushes. Handwritten in pencil on the lid of the cardboard box is the word,\" Brushes.\"  Blue and white label on end of box: Series 821 U.S.A. Made, Black \"J\" Sable Oil Artists's BRIGHTS 1/2 Dozen, Size SL.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"Gift of Juan and Anna Marie Hamilton","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Grumbacher, Inc.. Box of Paintbrushes, 20th Century. Cardboard, wood, metal and bristle, 14 1/2 x 3 x 1 1/2 inches. Georgia O'Keeffe Museum. Gift of Juan and Anna Marie Hamilton. © Unknown. [RC.1998.1.704]","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}